  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution for recruitment of DRR/R Coordinator and the DRR/R Working Group Phases 1-5</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRS, CAFOD, Caritas Australia and Tr&#xf3;caire have committed to a joint initiative, the DRR and Resilience Working Group (DRR/R WG) to strengthen their own capacity and that of partners in the development and implementation of DRR/R programming through building capacity ,providing practical support to field level implementation, promoting good practice and continual learning in relation to DRR/R and developing strategic links with the wider Caritas network. In the process of working together this will maximise the ability to influence and facilitate a more effective field work with partner&#x2019;s .The role of DRR/R coordinator will be to provide essential coordination and leadership for this initiative across the three organisations
CRS will coordinate and lead in recruitment process of DRR/R Coordinator, host and manage  the DRR/R coordinator. CAFOD and CA are responsible for participating in recruitment process ,providing feedback on performance of coordinator and meeting the broader set of requirements identified in the MOU
MOU amended and agreed by all parties (in April 2023) to extend the project for two more years, to 30 April 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
